Package: dev.airdevs.dsh-app
Name: DSH App (SpringBoard + KeepAlive)
Version: 0.2.1-rc.5+ios16
Section: Applications
Priority: optional
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Air-Devs <air2@localhost>
Depends: dev.airdevs.dsh (>= 0.2.1-rc.5+ios15)
Description: Installs a real SpringBoard app + a launchd-managed DSH daemon.
 This is the "IPA made into a deb" layout used by UTM / JBDev / Theos:
 an arm64 .app bundle is placed in /var/jb/Applications/DSH.app, the
 postinst pseudo-signs its executable with the on-device ldid (no Apple
 certificate needed), and uicache registers it so the icon appears on the
 Home Screen. Tapping the icon opens the DSH Web UI.
 The actual DSH host no longer depends on a terminal session: a
 LaunchDaemon (RunAtLoad + KeepAlive + ThrottleInterval) starts it at
 jailbreak time, restarts it the moment it is killed by jetsam, and keeps
 it alive after the terminal app is closed. Type `dsh` still works.
 dsh-app-ctl status|start|stop|restart|log|enable|disable manages it.
 Also ships the on-device phone-control toolchain: a pure-Node MCP server
 (127.0.0.1:8091, its own KeepAlive LaunchDaemon) plus an idempotent
 registration of the dsh-mcp-client config into $DSH_HOME patch files.
 Starting DSH by any means then exposes mcp__ios__* tools: device info,
 shell, files, app list/launch, URL schemes and DSH status work out of the
 box; screen/touch/OCR tools are forwarded to witchan/ios-mcp on 8090
 when that optional native service is running. Disable with
 dsh-phone-bridge-ctl config-off and dsh-phone-bridge-ctl disable.
 No Apple signing identity is used. Everything is plain files: plist,
 shell, one small arm64 Mach-O launcher, and PNG icons. Build is
 byte-reproducible from sh build-app.sh (SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH pinned).
Homepage: https://github.com/yitenchen123/dsh-ios
